  "notes": "Verified modern scholarly article Work published in Revue d'assyriologie 93 (2001), pages 39-66. It grounds a local archaeological and tablet-typological reconstruction of House F at Nippur. The Work is not House F itself, an ancient school organization, an excavation assemblage, a physical tablet, a curriculum, or transparent ethnography. The title's phrase 'A Scribal School' remains the article's scholarly framing, not an immutable ancient institutional identity. ISAC 2023 and Robson's 2026 return to House F remain later controls on locality, temporality, community, formation, and interpretation. Only bibliographic identity and an unreviewed source-reported authorship claim are admitted; no article payload, Expression, Edition, Item, archaeological membership, text, translation, semantic claim, graph relation, or canon state is created.",
